[00:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '[music] &gt;&gt; All right, YouTube. What is good? It\'s your boy Rebel back with another video. And today, we are taking a look at Sense Nova U 1.5 8B. So, Sense Nova 1.5 is'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Sense Nova\'s latest native unified multi-model checkpoint. This checkpoint provides more accuracy, consistency, it\'s more reliable, and aesthetically'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'compelling. The model is built on Neo Unify. So, this new release focuses on six user-visible improvements. Higher-quality image generation. So, you\'re getting improved composition and'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'color harmony with more realistic material rendering, natural lighting, stronger visual fidelity, and finer local details. You are now getting better text rendering and infographic generation. So, more legible Chinese and English text with clear information'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hierarchy in posters, infographics, brand assets, and other text-dense designs. It has more efficient native 4K generation. So, you get more coherent global structures, color harmony, and'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'stable high-resolution outputs. There is a more reliable native image editing portion of the model. So, you can use this model to either generate or edit your images. Although, I was unable to'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'get an edit out due to VRAM capabilities. My PC is just too small, and it was ooming for me no matter what I did. But, stronger complex instruction following. So, you get more consistent execution on object count, spatial'

[01:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'relationships, layouts, styles, and multiple constraints within a single request. And you get more precise visual control. So, you get more accurate region and object level control through bounding boxes, visual markers, and'

[01:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'single or multi-image references. Now, there is only one quantization available, and that is, of course, mine. So, when you get in here, you\'re going to be able to select anywhere from a Q2 to a Q8. The Q2 being about 9 GB, and'

[01:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the Q8 being about 21. The cool thing about this model is you don\'t need anything but the model itself. So, you don\'t need a text encoder, you don\'t need a VAE, you don\'t need anything'

[02:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'other than the model. The only other thing you may need is this eight-step Laura that has been provided from the Sensei Nova team as well for this model specifically. So, this is going to lower your step count from a minimum of 25'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'down to eight, which really speeds up generation time and helps force aesthetics. So, now there is a creator by the name of SM them. He has also released a few variations. Um you do'

[02:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'have an int 8 comrade at 18 GB, you have an FP8 at 18 GB, and then you have, you know, your SFT, you have, you know, your mergers if you\'d like to use those. This creator specifically has a node set for'

[02:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the model. So, if you\'re going to run his variations, you can use his node set. But, if you\'re going to run mine, you need my custom node set that forked off of his because his node set was curated specifically for his guffs, and'

[02:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'no other guffs feed into his pipeline. So, I had to fork it and do some editing for you guys to be able to use my guffs. It\'s a very simple get clone and install of these requirements for the node. Um other than that, the workflow is very'

[03:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'simple. So, when you get into comfy, it\'s just going to be a simple model node, a simple sampler node, and then a save image node. So, I will link everything in the description. The model\'s custom node set and a workflow'

[03:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'will be in the model repo, so you guys can grab that if you are confused as to what you\'re doing. But, it\'s just three simple nodes. Like I said before, the model does not require a text encoder or a VAE, so you can just plug in your guff'

[03:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in your Laura and get to work. The only thing you need to remember is that your guffs go in the guff folder, not your unet folder. You want it in your guff folder here. So, starting on the left'

[03:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here, we have our model node. So, if you are to run the intake com route or the FP8, you will use this diffusion models section, and your model will go in the diffusion models folder. If you don\'t, you will put your guff in the guff'

[04:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'folder, and you will put your Laura in the Laura folder, and they will both load from here. You also have an attention back end option, so you can select from flash or SDPA if you need to. I just leave it on auto. And then you have your sampler node. So, this is'

[04:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a very important part here to remember. If you are going to generate an image, you want it on edit. You do not want to put it on interleave or VQA. You want it on edit. It will generate your image.'

[04:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Trust me, just leave it on edit. The reason you want interleave is if you are working with an image and trying to bring text in, and then the VQA is something else that you\'re never going to use either. I would just leave this image mode on edit. And now, underneath'

[04:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that, you have your prompt node. You have your seed, your control for your seed, you have your step count, you have your target pixels, so you can select your resolution and aspect ratio that you would like. Then you have a CFG, you have an image CFG, and then you have a'

[04:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'time step shift, which you can leave this at three. Underneath that, you have a few things that you don\'t need to touch, your batch size, prefetch count, interleave max, and CFG norm. Um you really really can just leave all of'

[05:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'those the same. Um the only thing that you can change is your enhance. So, if you would like to use the onboard prompt enhance that is built into the model, you can do that. Um there\'s also a think mode and a sample mode. You can run a'

[05:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'preview. Then you have your max tokens, your temperature, your top P and K, and then you have repetition penalty. These are for your LLM enhanced think mode right here. So, if you don\'t use these, you don\'t need to worry about these. If'

[05:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you do use these, these will help you tune the LLM portion to get a good prompt. I will not be showcasing that though today cuz it is very time-consuming, and I recommend you just leave it off. And then we have our save image node on the right here, and that'

[05:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'literally accounts for the workflow. So, I\'m not going to waste any more time, and I will show you guys some examples as I know that\'s probably what you\'re here for. One thing though, before we get started on these examples, I want you guys to keep in mind, there is a'

[05:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'very strict prompting method to this model. Um prompting for anything like micro details or, you know, skin textures or rain or anything that\'s going to be a'

[06:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'fine detail that needs gen\'d is going to be overcompensated for, and you need to not use those tags specifically. So, for our first image here, we have an alien holding a sign reading Rebel Sins Nova'

[06:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '1.5. And here we have an alien taking a selfie in a bathroom. Pretty standard. Um no complaints here. The only thing I\'m going to say is placement is very weird for the objects'

[06:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in the room, and this is probably due to the fact that I did not specifically prompt for any of this, and it tried its best to fit it in the image to distinguish that this is a bathroom. Now, one of the things I did want to test was the infographic portion to see'

[06:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'if it had upgraded in any way, and from what I can tell, I did run the eight-step Laura for all of these generations, so we might not have had enough time to diffuse. But if you take'

[06:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a look at all of these examples, you\'ll notice every single one of them has a hallucination of text, and I did about 20 of these generations back-to-back. None of them came out clean. So, this is'

[07:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'something to keep in mind. If you thought this was going to be a valid source for infographics, it honestly is not yet. It\'s a slight improvement over the original variation of the model. Um'

[07:20] [scene:talk]
